From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Crescentm <guyues@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] mesh: restart peering when the driver lost a known peer

mac80211 sends NL80211_CMD_NEW_PEER_CANDIDATE for every matching beacon
from a mesh neighbour for which it has no station entry. wpa_supplicant
logs "new peer notification" and calls mesh_mpm_add_peer(), which returns
early without a message if a hostapd sta_info entry for the address
already exists.

Station removals done by the kernel are not reported for mesh interfaces
(nl80211_del_station_event() only handles AP SME and IBSS), so the two
can get out of sync: the kernel has no station, wpa_supplicant still has
one. The kernel then reports the peer again for every beacon, which only
shows up as a stream of "new peer notification" messages, and the peer is
not re-added until ap_handle_timer() notices the missing driver entry
after mesh_max_inactivity (300 s by default).

When a candidate is reported for a known peer, ask the driver whether it
still has the station. If it does not, log it, free the stale entry and
add the peer again.

Signed-off-by: Crescentm <guyues@outlook.com>
---
 wpa_supplicant/mesh_mpm.c | 26 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+)

diff --git a/wpa_supplicant/mesh_mpm.c b/wpa_supplicant/mesh_mpm.c
index 66684c9..6299315 100644
--- a/wpa_supplicant/mesh_mpm.c
+++ b/wpa_supplicant/mesh_mpm.c
@@ -17,6 +17,7 @@
 #include "ap/sta_info.h"
 #include "ap/ieee802_11.h"
 #include "ap/beacon.h"
+#include "ap/ap_drv_ops.h"
 #include "ap/wpa_auth.h"
 #include "wpa_supplicant_i.h"
 #include "driver_i.h"
@@ -848,6 +849,31 @@ void wpa_mesh_new_mesh_peer(struct wpa_supplicant *wpa_s, const u8 *addr,
 	struct sta_info *sta;
 	struct wpa_ssid *ssid = wpa_s->current_ssid;
 
+	/*
+	 * The driver reports a new peer candidate only while it has no
+	 * station entry for the peer. If we still have one, the driver has
+	 * dropped the station without telling us (station removal events are
+	 * not reported for mesh interfaces). mesh_mpm_add_peer() would then
+	 * ignore the peer and the driver would report it again for every
+	 * beacon until the inactivity timer cleans up. Drop the stale entry
+	 * so that peering can start over.
+	 */
+	sta = ap_get_sta(data, addr);
+	if (sta) {
+		if (hostapd_drv_get_inact_sec(data, addr) != -ENOENT) {
+			wpa_msg(wpa_s, MSG_DEBUG,
+				"mesh: Peer " MACSTR " is already known",
+				MAC2STR(addr));
+			return;
+		}
+
+		wpa_msg(wpa_s, MSG_INFO,
+			"mesh: Peer " MACSTR
+			" lost its driver entry - restart peering",
+			MAC2STR(addr));
+		ap_free_sta(data, sta);
+	}
+
 	sta = mesh_mpm_add_peer(wpa_s, addr, elems);
 	if (!sta)
 		return;
